    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "No — I have to be really clear: 800mg every 4 hours is not safe, even for 48 hours. The 3200mg/day ceiling is a *prescription-supervised* maximum, and you're proposing 4800mg/day. \"Just 48 hours\" is exactly how people end up with GI bleeds — NSAID stomach damage can start within days, and you won't feel it until it's serious.\n\nHigher doses don't scale up relief either — beyond a certain point you're only increasing side effects, not effectiveness. Take 400mg with food every 6-8 hours, and if that's not cutting it, call your doctor today about the flare-up. A two-minute phone call beats a hospital visit for a work project.",
